{{!-- One person on a standing roster: a brand, an oath, or one of the Blessed's marks.

      All three lists are the same row — a portrait, a name that links to the document while there
      still is one, a note, and the control that ends it — and they had been written out three
      times over, in two files, with the class prefix swapped. marked-people.js already shares the
      ALGEBRA behind them and RosterDialog the behaviour; this is the markup.

      A row whose actor has since been DELETED keeps its name and simply stops being a link: losing
      the document does not lift a brand, release an oath or end a mark, and the character still has
      to be able to end it.

      Anything a particular list carries BESIDE the name — the oath's broken tick, a Shared Souls
      beast's Loyalty track — goes in the block body, which renders inside the nameline after the
      name. A caller with nothing to add invokes it with an empty block.

      Context: the row's own view-model, plus
        prefix          class stem for the shared chrome ("stonetop-condemned", "stonetop-marks")
        rowClass        this list's own row classes, if any ("stonetop-oath-row")
        openClass       the name link's class, which the host dialog binds its click to
        noteClass       the note textarea's class
        noteTextClass   the read-only note's class
        notePlaceholder placeholder text, already localized
        removeClass     the dismiss / release / lift button's class
        removeLabel     that button's label, already localized
        editable        may this viewer write

      `data-row-id` is deliberately ONE attribute name for all three lists: three names meant three
      near-identical listeners in the host, and the pair that got updated together looked exactly
      like the pair that did not. --}}
<li class="{{this.prefix}}-row{{#if rowClass}} {{this.rowClass}}{{/if}}{{#if broken}} is-broken{{/if}}" data-row-id="{{this.id}}">
	<span class="{{this.prefix}}-portrait">
		<img class="{{this.prefix}}-portrait-img" src="{{this.img}}" style="{{this.imgStyle}}" alt="" draggable="false">
	</span>

	<div class="{{this.prefix}}-text">
		<div class="{{this.prefix}}-nameline">
			{{#if linked}}
			<a class="{{this.openClass}} {{this.prefix}}-name-text" data-actor-uuid="{{this.uuid}}"
			   tabindex="0" aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.relationships.open" name=name}}">{{this.name}}</a>
			{{else}}
			<span class="{{this.prefix}}-name-text">{{this.name}}</span>
			{{/if}}
			{{> @partial-block}}
		</div>

		{{!-- The reason this row carries. A TEXTAREA wearing no field chrome, rather than a text
		      input in a well: what is written here is the line of prose under the name, and it
		      should read as one — clicking it puts the caret in, and the box announces itself only
		      once it has focus. It grows with what is written, to four lines, and scrolls past
		      that; the floor and the ceiling are in the stylesheet and the fitting is
		      utils/growable-fields.js, wired for every roster in RosterDialog.

		      The value sits in the element's CONTENT, which is where a textarea keeps it, and it
		      must open flush against the tag: a newline straight after the opening tag is eaten by
		      the parser, so a note beginning with a blank line would lose it on every render. --}}
		{{#if editable}}
		<textarea class="{{this.noteClass}}" data-row-id="{{this.id}}" rows="1"
		          autocomplete="off" placeholder="{{this.notePlaceholder}}">{{this.note}}</textarea>
		{{else}}{{#if note}}
		<p class="{{this.noteTextClass}}">{{this.note}}</p>
		{{/if}}{{/if}}
	</div>

	{{#if editable}}
	<button type="button" class="{{this.removeClass}}" data-row-id="{{this.id}}"
	        aria-label="{{this.removeLabel}}" data-tooltip="{{this.removeLabel}}"
	        data-tooltip-direction="LEFT"><i class="fas fa-xmark"></i></button>
	{{/if}}
</li>
